-- claude-opus-48-dynamic-workflows
UPDATE news SET body = '<p>Anthropic launched <strong>Claude Opus 4.8</strong> on May 28, 2026 — just 41 days after Opus 4.7. The release is positioned as a significant quality-of-life update: faster responses, better long-context consistency, and a dramatic jump in mathematical reasoning.</p>

    <h2>Math benchmark: 69.3% to 96.7%</h2>
    <p>The most striking improvement is on <strong>USAMO 2026</strong> — the USA Mathematical Olympiad benchmark. Opus 4.8 scores <strong>96.7%</strong>, up from 69.3% on Opus 4.7. That is a 27-point jump in 41 days, making Opus 4.8 the strongest publicly available model on advanced mathematics.</p>
    <p>Opus 4.8 is also roughly <strong>four times less likely</strong> to let flaws in its own code pass without flagging them, and proactively signals uncertainty rather than confidently hallucinating.</p>

    <h2>Dynamic Workflows in Claude Code</h2>
    <p>The biggest agentic feature is <strong>Dynamic Workflows</strong>: Claude Code can now plan a large task, spin up up to <strong>1,000 parallel subagents</strong>, distribute the work across them, and verify outputs against your test suite — all without human intervention. The feature is designed for repository-scale migrations and hundreds-of-thousands-of-lines-of-code refactors that would previously require a team of engineers.</p>

    <h2>Pricing: same base, cheaper Fast mode</h2>
    <p>Standard pricing holds at <strong>$5 per million input tokens and $25 per million output tokens</strong> — identical to Opus 4.7. The big change is in Fast mode: it drops from <strong>$30/$150</strong> per million tokens (Opus 4.7) to <strong>$10/$50</strong> — a 3× cost reduction for latency-sensitive workloads. Prompt caching brings savings up to 90%; batch processing offers 50% off.</p>
    <p>Opus 4.8 is available in Claude.ai for Pro, Max, Team, and Enterprise subscribers, and via the Anthropic API, AWS Bedrock, Google Cloud Vertex AI, and Microsoft Foundry.</p>

    <h2>Mythos Preview coming soon</h2>
    <p>Separately, Anthropic confirmed that <strong>Claude Mythos Preview</strong> — the restricted-access cybersecurity model — will be available to approved organizations "in the coming weeks." During its 30-day preview, Mythos and ~50 partner organizations identified more than 10,000 high- or critical-severity vulnerabilities in systemically important software.</p>
  </div>
